[Replicate](https://replicate.com/) runs open-source machine learning models in the cloud. You call a model by name through its API and pay for the compute the prediction uses, without managing GPUs yourself.

# How does the integration work?

The **Generate with Replicate** function template puts three Replicate models behind one Appwrite Function. Send it a prompt and an output type, and it runs the matching model:

| `type` | Model | Settings in the template |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `text` | `meta/llama-2-70b-chat` | Up to 512 new tokens |
| `image` | `stability-ai/sdxl` | 512 x 512 pixels, with a negative prompt |
| `audio` | `meta/musicgen` | 30 seconds of audio |

`GET /` serves a demo form, and `POST /` returns `{"ok": true, "response": ..., "type": ...}`, where `response` is the generated text, or the URL of the generated image or audio file. Your Replicate token stays in the function, so your app can call it directly.

# Prerequisites

- A [Replicate account](https://replicate.com/) with billing set up. Replicate charges for the compute each prediction uses.

# How to implement

To implement the Replicate integration, there are several steps you must complete:

## Step 1: Create a Replicate API token

Open the [API tokens page](https://replicate.com/account/api-tokens) in your Replicate account and create a token. Tokens start with `r8_`.

## Step 2: Create the Appwrite Function

For this step, you must [create an account on Appwrite Cloud](/sign-up) if you haven't already. In the Appwrite Console, go to **Functions**, open the **Templates** tab, search for **Generate with Replicate**, and click **Create from template**. Under **Template variables**, set `REPLICATE_API_TOKEN` to your token.

Choose **Connect your repository** to clone the template into a Git repository you can edit later, for example to swap models, or **Connect later** to deploy it right away. Then click **Create and deploy**.

## Step 3: Generate content

Copy the function's domain from the **Domains** tab and open it in your browser to use the demo form, or send a request:

```bash
curl -X POST https://<FUNCTION_DOMAIN> \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"prompt": "Write a haiku about Mondays", "type": "text"}'
```

Change `type` to `image` or `audio` to run the other models. A missing `prompt` or an unknown `type` returns a `400` error.

Requests to a function's domain are [synchronous executions](/docs/products/functions/execute#synchronous-executions), which stop after 30 seconds. Slower predictions, such as generating music, can run past that limit, so test each output type you plan to use.

The template allows anyone to execute the function, so anyone who finds its domain can run Replicate models with your token. Before you use it in a public app, replace `Any` in the function's [execute access](/docs/products/functions/functions#execution-access) with narrower [roles](/docs/advanced/security/permissions#permission-roles), such as `Users`, and call the function [with an Appwrite SDK](/docs/products/functions/execute#sdk) instead of its domain.

